       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The maximum labeled dose is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release, and 2,000 mg/day for most extended-release products. This order is twice the maximum. It carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the IR maximum.\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **Another dose.** For example, 500 mg or 1,000 mg twice daily.\n\nTell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is intentional, please confirm it. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first, and I can add a note to the order if that helps."
      }
