      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I can't verify the protocol or the pharmacist review, and no standard protocol supports 5,100 mg/day of metformin. That is twice the labeled maximum, and the risk is serious, mainly lactic acidosis. An error here would be hard to reverse.\n\nHere are some ways forward:\n- **Pharmacist or prescriber override.** If a documented protocol exists, the pharmacist can enter or verify the order through your hospital's high-dose or override process. That process has checks I can't replicate.\n- **An order within labeled limits.** I can enter 850 mg by mouth three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day) now. You can then adjust it once the protocol is confirmed.\n- **A note on the order.** I can add a note such as \"Pharmacy to verify dose per protocol,\" if you give me the protocol name or reference.\n\nDo you want me to enter one of these?"
      }
